WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:16.064
Unit four: Passion Projects. Today you will talk about ongoing actions with the present perfect continuous.

4
00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:18.865
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.161
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:25.331
Personal initiative.

7
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.605
Personal initiative means starting something by yourself.

8
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:33.064
She showed personal initiative and started a club.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.697
Your turn. Say: Personal initiative.

10
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:40.987
Personal initiative.

11
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.925
Creative venture.

12
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:47.124
Creative venture means a new creative project or business.

13
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:50.111
Our comic book is a creative venture.

14
00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.427
Your turn. Say: Creative venture.

15
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.581
Creative venture.

16
00:00:58.317 --> 00:00:59.562
Side project.

17
00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:04.105
Side project means a project you do besides school or work.

18
00:01:04.717 --> 00:01:06.902
My side project is a cooking blog.

19
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:10.587
Your turn. Say: Side project.

20
00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:14.794
Side project.

21
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.981
Skill-building.

22
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:21.225
Skill-building means developing your abilities.

23
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:24.443
Coding camps are great for skill-building.

24
00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.923
Your turn. Say: Skill-building.

25
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.557
Skill-building.

26
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:34.353
Portfolio.

27
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.139
Portfolio means a collection of your best work.

28
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.738
Put your designs in a portfolio.

29
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.944
Your turn. Say: Portfolio.

30
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.998
Portfolio.

31
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.192
Experimentation.

32
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:54.797
Experimentation means trying new ideas to see what works.

33
00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:57.615
Experimentation is part of learning.

34
00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:01.066
Your turn. Say: Experimentation.

35
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.365
Experimentation.

36
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:07.512
Self-motivated.

37
00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:12.095
Self-motivated means working hard without being told.

38
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:15.507
Self-motivated students finish their projects.

39
00:02:16.117 --> 00:02:19.152
Your turn. Say: Self-motivated.

40
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.547
Self-motivated.

41
00:02:24.283 --> 00:02:25.702
Innovative idea.

42
00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:29.680
Innovative idea means a new and clever idea.

43
00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.759
Her innovative idea won the science fair.

44
00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.258
Your turn. Say: Innovative idea.

45
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.484
Innovative idea.

46
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.239
Prototype.

47
00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.120
Prototype means the first test model of something.

48
00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:49.065
We built a prototype of a solar fan.

49
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.047
Your turn. Say: Prototype.

50
00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.017
Prototype.

51
00:02:56.783 --> 00:02:58.040
Showcase work.

52
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.688
Showcase work means to show your work to others.

53
00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:04.445
We showcase work at the end of term.

54
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.737
Your turn. Say: Showcase work.

55
00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.740
Showcase work.

56
00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:13.902
Collaborative effort.

57
00:03:14.917 --> 00:03:17.868
Collaborative effort means work done together as a team.

58
00:03:18.483 --> 00:03:20.541
The mural was a collaborative effort.

59
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.569
Your turn. Say: Collaborative effort.

60
00:03:27.433 --> 00:03:28.678
Collaborative effort.

61
00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:30.453
Passion-driven.

62
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.634
Passion-driven means pushed forward by strong interest.

63
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.598
Passion-driven projects are the most fun.

64
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.569
Your turn. Say: Passion-driven.

65
00:03:43.433 --> 00:03:44.574
Passion-driven.

66
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.983
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.817 --> 00:03:51.793
Visal, do you have a side project?

68
00:03:52.883 --> 00:03:56.557
Yes! I have been working on this project for months.

69
00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.732
What is it?

70
00:03:59.817 --> 00:04:04.141
A smart watering system. I have been testing a prototype at home.

71
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.215
That's an innovative idea!

72
00:04:08.317 --> 00:04:12.409
Thanks. I have been adding photos to my portfolio, too.

73
00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.299
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.194
Grammar focus: Present perfect continuous.

75
00:04:19.494 --> 00:04:20.670
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:21.383 --> 00:04:23.731
I have been working on this project for months.

77
00:04:24.617 --> 00:04:26.616
She has been learning guitar since May.

78
00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:29.865
We have been building a prototype all week.

79
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:38.259
Use this tense for an action that started in the past and is still going on. Use 'for' with a period and 'since' with a starting point.

80
00:04:39.017 --> 00:04:42.551
Be careful! Don't say: I have been work on this for months.

81
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.219
Say: I have been working on this for months.

82
00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.600
After 'have been', use the -ing form.

83
00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:53.377
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:55.702
My Passion Project.

85
00:04:56.002 --> 00:04:59.023
I have been working on a creative venture since January.

86
00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:03.414
It is a side project about Khmer folk tales for children.

87
00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.537
I have been drawing pictures and building a website prototype.

88
00:05:08.533 --> 00:05:12.286
This skill-building project has helped my portfolio grow.

89
00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.147
Next month, I will showcase work at the school fair.

90
00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:21.502
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.280
I have been blank this for months.

92
00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.595
A, doing. B, do. C, done.

93
00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:33.237
The answer is A: doing.

94
00:05:34.383 --> 00:05:36.743
The first test model of something is a blank.

95
00:05:37.043 --> 00:05:40.917
A, prototype. B, portfolio. C, venture.

96
00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.536
The answer is A: prototype.

97
00:05:47.683 --> 00:05:49.927
A collection of your best work is a blank.

98
00:05:50.227 --> 00:05:54.739
A, portfolio. B, prototype. C, showcase.

99
00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.961
The answer is A: portfolio.

100
00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.260
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:06.117 --> 00:06:08.511
What passion project would you like to start?

102
00:06:17.317 --> 00:06:18.817
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:19.117 --> 00:06:28.329
I would like to start a photography project about my village. I have been taking photos on my phone for a year, and I want to showcase my work online.

104
00:06:28.629 --> 00:06:30.327
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:31.217 --> 00:06:36.028
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present perfect continuous.

106
00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:40.095
Today's value is passion. Find what you love and practise it.

107
00:06:40.395 --> 00:06:42.978
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

108
00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:46.395
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

